│  └───────────┬────────────┘  │          │  └───────────▲────────────┘  │
└──────────────┼───────────────┘          └──────────────┼───────────────┘
               │ write ct                 read ct        │
               ▼                                          │
   ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   UNTRUSTED: SHARED FILE EDGE (project dir, .hacp-secure/<sid>/…)
   · observer can read  → ciphertext only (confidentiality)
   · writer can inject  → tag/signature failure (authenticity)
   · replayer can replay→ seq window rejects; replay state is
     guardian-memory-only, so edge tampering cannot roll it back
   · attacker deletes an envelope → SequenceGap hard abort (loud,
     never a silent stall); bounded gap-hold queue drains reorders
   · attacker strips sig/AEAD → DowngradeDetected, session abort
     (security mode comes from peers.json policy, NOT from traffic)
   · drops/duplicates   → at-least-once edge; duplicates dropped+audited
   · NO security state persists here: no counters, no keys, no pins
   ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

   DEGRADED MODE (hackathon laptop, same uid for agent+guardian):
   the uid wall above is ABSENT; protection reduces to context hygiene
   (no tool ever returns key material). Labeled at startup. Residual risk.
```

